# Only meaningful at scale 1.0: wrench emulates a device pixel scale by pushing a
# root reference frame with a scale transform, and a bitmap-strike run rasterizes at
# its transform's scale (bug 2064316), so at other scales the test rasterizes at the
# emulated scale while the reference stays at the 1.0 it names. Gecko's real device
# pixel scale is not a transform, so nothing is lost there.
scale(1.0) fuzzy(1,20) platform(linux) == bitmap-glyph-transform.yaml bitmap-glyph-transform-ref.yaml
# bug 2061411 / 2062234: a scale transform, uniform or not, must reach an
# embedded-bitmap glyph. bug 2064316: it must reach the rasterizer as well, so the
# glyph is rendered at its final size instead of being scaled up from the
# untransformed one. FreeType-only (the bitmap strike selection), so linux, and
# scale 1.0 only for the same reason as bitmap-glyph-transform above.
scale(1.0) platform(linux) == 2061411-bitmap-scale.yaml 2061411-bitmap-scale-ref.yaml
