# bug 2056856: a device-space text run must round its *ancestor* clips out on the
# sub-pixel (horizontal) axis, not keep them exact. Proggy's ppem-11 bitmap strike
# places a bearing-0 glyph on the device grid with no sub-pixel positioning; an
# exact fractional left edge on an ancestor clip-chain node shaves its leftmost
# column. FreeType-only (the bitmap strike selection), so restrict to linux.
# Only meaningful at scale 1.0: wrench emulates a device pixel scale by pushing a
# root reference frame with a scale transform, and a bitmap font under any scale
# transform now rasterizes in local space (bug 2061411), so at other scales the
# glyphs are no longer device-grid-placed and this asserts nothing. Gecko's real
# device pixel scale is not a transform, so the device path still applies there.
scale(1.0) platform(linux) == 2056856-bitmap-clip.yaml 2056856-bitmap-clip-ref.yaml

# bug 2056856: a glyph from an embedded bitmap strike ignores the sub-pixel offset
# its key asks for, so its pen must round to nearest rather than floor with the
# sub-pixel bias, which would drag it up to 0.875px left of where it was placed.
# Each row is drawn at a fractional x and referenced at round(x). The pen rounds
# in *device* space, so the reference position is only expressible at one scale -
# at scale 2 the same layout x has a different fraction and rounds the other way.
# FreeType-only (the bitmap strike selection), so restrict to linux.
scale(1.0) platform(linux) == 2056856-bitmap-pen.yaml 2056856-bitmap-pen-ref.yaml
